!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/validate/valid/a-type-value-in-data-may-state-bounds-that-cross-expected.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/validate-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §4.2, [TSON-SCHEMA] §5.7"
  description: """
    Bounds that cross are a declaration's rule, and a value of a kernel type written as data declares nothing:
    `min_items` and `max_items` are each a `numeric.count`, and 5 and 2 each are one, so the array is valid data.
    The same bounds in a schema declaration are refused (class2/schema/invalid/container-bounds-that-admit-nothing).
    """
  valid: _
}
